From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] frontends/cmn: give both QoS tags of a ported connection a
 value

ecm_ported_ipv{4,6}_process() collects the classifiers' verdict in a
struct ecm_classifier_process_response on the stack. Since cc610c8 ("Add
per-direction acceleration and classification support for UDP flows") a
uni-direction connection, which every UDP connection is by default
(unidir_accel_en=1), sets only the sending direction's QoS tag. Since
6c84102 ("Allocate memory dynamically for PPE FE update rule message")
the struct is no longer zeroed. The flow tag is written to skb->priority
for a packet of either direction, so a reply packet gets uninitialised
stack as its priority whenever no classifier supplies a QoS tag: the DSCP
classifier is off, or leaves the connection (no conntrack, no DSCPREMARK
extension, a failed or denied offload).

On the host Wi-Fi path that priority becomes the frame's TID: ath11k
takes skb->priority & 0xf with TID override, and mac80211's 802.3 path
does not re-classify the frame. A routed UDP download into a Wi-Fi client
then asserts the WLAN firmware (ar_wal_tx_send.c:22193, WLAN_TX_DE).
Measured on a Xiaomi AX3000T v2 (IPQ5018 + QCN6122) in host Wi-Fi mode,
with an nft counter after ECM's hook: 369 packets of a UDP download left
with a priority set, 349 of them above 7, and the 5 GHz firmware
asserted. With unidir_accel_en=0, 240009 packets left with none set and
nothing asserted.

Give both tags the packet's own priority again, as before cc610c8. A
connection accelerated in both directions is unchanged. A packet of a
uni-direction connection keeps its own priority, so the write back to
skb->priority does nothing to it. Restoring the zero initialiser instead
would set the priority of every uni-direction reply packet to 0, dropping
the one ip_forward() derives from its TOS.

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/frontends/cmn/ecm_ported_ipv4.c
+++ b/frontends/cmn/ecm_ported_ipv4.c
@@ -1033,22 +1033,14 @@ done:
 	prevalent_pr.drop = false;
 
 	/*
-	 * In case of uni-direction acceleration, assign priority per direction
+	 * Give both tags this packet's priority, for a uni-direction connection
+	 * too: the flow tag is written to skb->priority below for a packet of
+	 * either direction. A classifier that sets a QoS tag overrides both.
 	 */
-	if (ci->unidir_accel_en) {
-		if (sender == ECM_TRACKER_SENDER_TYPE_SRC) {
-			prevalent_pr.flow_qos_tag = skb->priority;
-			prevalent_pr.flow_int_pri = 0;	/* skb->int_pri requires QSDK kernel patches */
-		} else {
-			prevalent_pr.return_qos_tag = skb->priority;
-			prevalent_pr.return_int_pri = 0;	/* skb->int_pri requires QSDK kernel patches */
-		}
-	} else {
-		prevalent_pr.flow_qos_tag = skb->priority;
-		prevalent_pr.return_qos_tag = skb->priority;
-		prevalent_pr.flow_int_pri = 0;	/* skb->int_pri requires QSDK kernel patches */
-		prevalent_pr.return_int_pri = 0;	/* skb->int_pri requires QSDK kernel patches */
-	}
+	prevalent_pr.flow_qos_tag = skb->priority;
+	prevalent_pr.return_qos_tag = skb->priority;
+	prevalent_pr.flow_int_pri = 0;	/* skb->int_pri requires QSDK kernel patches */
+	prevalent_pr.return_int_pri = 0;	/* skb->int_pri requires QSDK kernel patches */
 
 	prevalent_pr.accel_mode = ECM_CLASSIFIER_ACCELERATION_MODE_ACCEL;
 	prevalent_pr.timer_group = ci_orig_timer_group = ecm_db_connection_timer_group_get(ci);
--- a/frontends/cmn/ecm_ported_ipv6.c
+++ b/frontends/cmn/ecm_ported_ipv6.c
@@ -1060,22 +1060,14 @@ done:
 	prevalent_pr.drop = false;
 
 	/*
-	 * In case of uni-direction acceleration, assign priority per direction.
+	 * Give both tags this packet's priority, for a uni-direction connection
+	 * too: the flow tag is written to skb->priority below for a packet of
+	 * either direction. A classifier that sets a QoS tag overrides both.
 	 */
-	if (ci->unidir_accel_en) {
-		if (sender == ECM_TRACKER_SENDER_TYPE_SRC) {
-			prevalent_pr.flow_qos_tag = skb->priority;
-			prevalent_pr.flow_int_pri = 0;	/* skb->int_pri requires QSDK kernel patches */
-		} else {
-			prevalent_pr.return_qos_tag = skb->priority;
-			prevalent_pr.return_int_pri = 0;	/* skb->int_pri requires QSDK kernel patches */
-		}
-	} else {
-		prevalent_pr.flow_qos_tag = skb->priority;
-		prevalent_pr.return_qos_tag = skb->priority;
-		prevalent_pr.flow_int_pri = 0;	/* skb->int_pri requires QSDK kernel patches */
-		prevalent_pr.return_int_pri = 0;	/* skb->int_pri requires QSDK kernel patches */
-	}
+	prevalent_pr.flow_qos_tag = skb->priority;
+	prevalent_pr.return_qos_tag = skb->priority;
+	prevalent_pr.flow_int_pri = 0;	/* skb->int_pri requires QSDK kernel patches */
+	prevalent_pr.return_int_pri = 0;	/* skb->int_pri requires QSDK kernel patches */
 
 	prevalent_pr.accel_mode = ECM_CLASSIFIER_ACCELERATION_MODE_ACCEL;
 	prevalent_pr.timer_group = ci_orig_timer_group = ecm_db_connection_timer_group_get(ci);
